      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lehigh was originally named Boone before being renamed after the coal-mining district in the Lehigh Valley of Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=LE011"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lehigh began as a mining camp in 1877 after J. Davis discovered coal in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=LE011"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Three different railroad lines once served Lehigh, making the town a major transportation hub by 1905.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
